          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=alexander.klimetschek",
            "name": "alexander.klimetschek",
            "key": "alexander.klimetschek",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443"
            },
            "displayName": "Alexander Klimetschek",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "body": "Although the exception might not be specific hinting on the error, IMHO this is correct behaviour. A node can only be locked once it is saved: see JCR 1.0 spec (or javadocs), 8.4.11 Node.lock: \"An InvalidItemStateException  is thrown if this node has pending unsaved changes.\" In the context of transactions, validity checks and persistence moves from the save() method to the commit of the transaction.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=alexander.klimetschek",
            "name": "alexander.klimetschek",
            "key": "alexander.klimetschek",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443"
            },
            "displayName": "Alexander Klimetschek",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "created": "2008-05-30T22:30:09.490+0000",
          "updated": "2008-05-30T22:30:09.490+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12397184/comment/12601341",
          "id": "12601341",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rpuch",
            "name": "rpuch",
            "key": "rpuch",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rpuch&avatarId=48468",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rpuch&avatarId=48468",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rpuch&avatarId=48468",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rpuch&avatarId=48468"
            },
            "displayName": "Roman Puchkovskiy",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Samara"
          },
          "body": "Node is actually saved (session.save() in one test, testRootNode.save() in the another). Yes, it's not _persisted_ immediately, but for the caller who is in this transaction this should look like as there's no any transaction. So I don't see what is incorrect here.\nFor instance, for versioning and checkin() there's same situation: you cannot checkin a node with unsaved changes, but node which was just created and saved still may be checked in in a transaction. Following test passes, while its only difference is that it uses checkin() instead of lock():\n\n    public void testCheckinInTx() throws Exception {\n        UserTransaction tx = new UserTransactionImpl(superuser);\n        tx.begin();\n        Node n = testRootNode.addNode(nodeName1);\n        n.addMixin(mixVersionable);\n        testRootNode.save();\n        n.checkin();\n        tx.commit();\n    }",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rpuch",
            "name": "rpuch",
            "key": "rpuch",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rpuch&avatarId=48468",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rpuch&avatarId=48468",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rpuch&avatarId=48468",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rpuch&avatarId=48468"
            },
            "displayName": "Roman Puchkovskiy",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Samara"
          },
          "created": "2008-05-31T04:47:53.531+0000",
          "updated": "2008-05-31T04:47:53.531+0000"
        },
        {
